16	 * parse it. One file, one declaration, is the fix this test pins.
17	 *
18	 * Three things about the merged workflow are easy to lose in an edit and expensive
19	 * to lose in production, so they are pinned here rather than left to a reader:
20	 *
21	 * - the jobs are chained by `needs`, and `apply-to-self` names BOTH of its
22	 *   predecessors, because the tag it announces is `release`'s output and GitHub
23	 *   exposes outputs only to a job that names their job directly;
24	 * - the merge waits for the required check to EXIST before watching anything.
25	 *   The validator writes it as its last act, after CI has concluded, so on a
26	 *   fresh pull request the deciding check does not exist yet, and a merge fired
27	 *   when the visible checks are green races that write and loses (measured: the
28	 *   base branch policy refused the merge);
